From f3635097d6ff2206c51bb62b0858b33538df6596 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gradic76 <gordan.radic@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 16:13:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] The Bell: audio-only, PCM and MP3 only
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Bell post-processes speech: it reads and writes WAV and MP3 and nothing else,
so the cut is narrower than NBR's, which has to open any audiobook.

ffmpeg: --disable-everything, then only the PCM and MP3 decoders and encoders,
the wav/w64/mp3/null muxers, and the audio filter list. libmp3lame is the one
external library kept — Bell exports MP3 and the encoder alone cannot write a
file without the muxer, so both are named.

mpv: the audio-only option set, every name checked against mpv's own
meson.options before it was written (43 video options left on 'auto' once
produced a video-capable 'audio-only' build).

Dropped from ffmpeg: gpl/version3 (no x264/x265 left to need them), avisynth,
vapoursynth, nvenc/nvdec/cuda/amf, openal, opengl, vaapi, and every remaining
--enable-lib*.
